<title>USA: UAL plans 2nd daily Chicago-London flight.</title>
<headline>UAL plans 2nd daily Chicago-London flight.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>UAL Corp's United Airlines said Monday it planned to launch a second daily flight linking Chicago's O'Hare and London's Heathrow airports.</p>
<p>The move follows approval by the British and U.S. governments for additional service on the route.</p>
<p>United expects to operate the second daily flight, aboard a 206-seat aircraft, between April 1 and October 25.</p>
<p>United's existing daily flight is aboard a 292-seat aircraft.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
